# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) if you want to change any of these. Everything is optional: the value shown is the default. No secret belongs in this file.

# Which back end the screens talk to (D-089). http = a running caw-back — the default, so a plain `bun run dev` is the real app; if caw-back is
# not reachable the screen says so, with the command to start it. mock = built-in sample data for team checks and the tests (`bun run dev:mock`).
CAW_API=http
# Where caw-back listens. Only read when CAW_API=http.
CAW_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4500
# Where "open this part in Blueprint" points: blueprint-front.
BLUEPRINT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3100
# The port of `bun run dev` and `bun run start`. 3500 is the one Blueprint's "ส่งไปสร้างที่ CAW" button opens.
PORT=3500
# Tests only (Playwright's web server sets it): lets POST /test-reset put the mock back to its seed. Leave unset otherwise.
# CAW_TEST_RESET=1
